nodecode-alans-way is a rewrite of capthvnsen's capthvnsen/alans-way-agents:

  https://github.com/capthvnsen/alans-way-agents
  commit 23cce292c867a42ccf9853b99d798add028788f0
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Alan's Way contributors (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the alans-way-computer plugin's transport to the Alan's Workspace
router became a Nodecode cell instead of a Hermes computer_use backend. The
same router tools (workspace_computer_apps, workspace_computer_snapshot,
workspace_computer_screenshot, workspace_computer_action,
workspace_computer_launch, cua_alans_way_status) are called with the same
arguments, and the gestural vocabulary is the original's: numbered controls
from a capture, press/double_click/right_click by ref or by point, drag
types/keys/scrolls, set_value for a field, focus_app to aim and launch. The
section, the tools and their descriptions, the primer and /computer are
Nodecode's own seams.

Left out: Hermes's ComputerUseBackend API, the one long-lived router child
multiplexed by request id (each call here starts, initializes, calls and
closes one), the delta merge of an action's reply into the held element list
(the reply is described and a fresh capture is asked for), the screenshot
pixel/point conversion for element bounds, the numeric overlay coverage
heuristic, the inferred error-code table beyond the router's own code, and
the permission-mode plumbing, which belonged to the Hermes tool rather than
to this backend.
